To celebrate the launch of the iPhone Duo this Friday, Apple has set up oversized iPhone Duo promotional displays at Apple Fifth Avenue in New York City, Apple Covent Garden in London, Apple BKC in India, and Apple Jing'an in Shanghai.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/10/Apple-Jing-an-iPhone-Duo-Displays.jpg" alt="" width="1600" height="900" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1072268" /><br/>
The installations were <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/10/22/giant-iphone-duo-apple-fifth-avenue/">already spotted under wraps</a>, and Apple CEO John Ternus has since revealed what they look like in a photo of Apple Jing'an shared <a href="https://weibo.com/n/JohnTernus">on his Weibo account</a> today. The oversized iPhone Duo displays have mirrored finishes and glowing edges, and they show the device in various positions, or poses as Apple calls them.<br/>
<br/>
Ternus is expected to be at Apple Fifth Avenue for iPhone Duo launch day. Apple said that its stores in the U.S. and select other countries will have <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/10/21/apple-stores-limited-iphone-duo-for-walk-in/">"limited" availability of the iPhone Duo</a> for walk-in customers tomorrow.<br/>
